<title>AUSTRALIA: ANZ appoints new chief financial officer.</title>
<headline>ANZ appoints new chief financial officer.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia and New Zealand Banking Group Ltd (ANZ) said on Tuesday it had appointed Peter Marriott, currently group general manager of credit and risk management, as its new chief financial officer.</p>
<p>Marriott will take up his new position on July 1, after the retirement of David Craig, the bank said.</p>
<p>ANZ executive director Alistair Maitland will retire on June 30, it also said.</p>
<p>-- Melbourne bureau 613-9286-1421</p>
